  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Maritime Decarbonisation and Green Shipping Program for Turkiye</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contract related to: Maritime Decarbonisation and Green Shipping Program for Turkiye - This action prioritises three areas of support: Enhancement of Ministry of Energy&#xBF;s capacities on efficient heating and cooling in order to contribute to the shift towards a resource-efficient, digitalised, smart, safe and sustainable low-carbon economy in Turkey. Secondly, strengthening the energy performance of public building stock through sustainable strategies aiming to improve the energy performance of the existing building stock in order to decrease the public expenditures on energy consumptions. Finally, the action will finance the Maritime Decarbonisation and Green Shipping Programme, which will target developing sustainable pilot projects involving ports, vessels, and the usage of alternative fuel in the Turkish Maritime Sector with the main obejetive of reducing GHG and air emissions, whilst supporting climate reliance investments promoting energy efficiency, electrification, circular economy and other environmental benefits.</narrative>
  </description>
